{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed218530468/13/codegen_prompts/3.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed218530468/13`\n- 题号：`3`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed218530468/13/3.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"3\">\n- `description`：沿彩色 L 形箭头指示的方向传播颜色信号，信号穿过双色中继站时变换颜色，最终将目标格着色为变换后的颜色。\n- `Input structure`：背景为 black。网格中有以下元素：\n  - 若干\"箭头\"对象：每个箭头由 3 个同色像素组成，排列为一个 1x2 的横条或竖条，其中一端额外附带一个垂直于条方向的 1 像素突出（形成 L 形），突出的反方向即箭头的发射方向。箭头的整体颜色为其信号的初始颜色。\n  - 若干\"中继站\"：每个中继站是一个 1x2 或 2x1 的双色像素对，两个像素颜色不同。中继站的朝向（水平或垂直）与它所服务的射线方向一致。中继站表示颜色映射：信号到达时若颜色与中继站某一端颜色匹配，则信号颜色变为另一端的颜色。\n  - 若干\"目标格\"：用 grey 单像素标记。\n  - 所有元素之间有足够的 black 间距。\n- `Rule`：\n  1. 从每个箭头出发，沿箭头发射方向发射一条直线射线，射线携带箭头颜色作为当前信号颜色。\n  2. 射线沿直线传播，遇到的第一个非 black 对象决定后续行为：\n     - 若遇到中继站：检查当前信号颜色是否与中继站两种颜色之一匹配。若匹配，信号颜色变为中继站的另一种颜色，射线继续沿原方向传播。若不匹配，射线终止。\n     - 若遇到目标格（grey 像素）：将该 grey 像素重新着色为当前信号颜色，射线终止。\n     - 若遇到网格边界或其他箭头：射线终止，无效果。\n  3. 射线经过的路径上不绘制任何痕迹，仅目标格被着色。移除所有箭头对象，保留中继站和未被命中的 grey 目标格。\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要先从 L 形结构识别箭头的发射方向（突出方向的反方向），然后追踪射线路径上中继站对颜色的级联变换——同一个初始颜色经过不同中继站链条后可能变为完全不同的最终颜色。理解中继站的双色结构是\"输入色 -> 输出色\"的可逆映射表是核心洞见。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：train/db7260a4, train/5adee1b2, train/320afe60, train/2f767503, train/5623160b, train/9344f635, train/d968ffd4, train/a09f6c25\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"db7260a4\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.4233\nmechanism=0.5137\nlexical=0.0101\ncode_feature=0.6000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:ray_loop, object:grid_edge, object:hole, object:line_segment, object:marker, object:path, object:sprite, operation:ray_cast, relation:between, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/db7260a4.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/db7260a4.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nDrop the singleton marker into the matching red U-shaped container, or make a bottom-row puddle if no closed container is hit.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has a dominant background, one singleton marker pixel on the top row,\n  and one other foreground color forming vertical bars and bottom segments.\n- A closed container is a U shape: two vertical side bars with a continuous\n  bottom segment between them and an empty rectangular interior above the bottom.\n\nRule\n- Remove the top marker from its original cell.\n- If exactly one closed U-shaped container has the marker column within its\n  horizontal footprint, fill that container's empty interior with the marker color.\n- If no closed container is under the marker column, fill the whole bottom row\n  with the marker color.\n\nKey insight\n- The marker does not identify a color by value; it identifies a vertical drop\n  column, and only a structurally closed U shape can catch and contain the fill.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"singleton top-row marker pixel\",\n  \"path\": \"vertical drop down the marker column; a closed U-shaped wall container catches the drop when the marker column lies within its horizontal footprint, otherwise the path reaches the bottom edge\",\n  \"dst\": \"closed U-shaped container interior, or the bottom row if no closed container catches the drop\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"fill the caught container's background interior with the marker color; if uncaught, fill the whole bottom row\",\n  \"transform\": \"erase the original marker pixel and keep all wall pixels unchanged\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"5adee1b2\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.4065\nmechanism=0.4888\nlexical=0.0104\ncode_feature=0.6000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:ray_loop, object:grid_edge, object:hole, object:line_segment, object:marker, object:sprite, operation:draw_line, operation:recolor, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5adee1b2.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/5adee1b2.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nUse the left-edge color legend to draw a padded rectangular halo around each matching object while preserving enclosed holes.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has a dominant background color.\n- One or more two-row markers sit on the left edge; each marker is a 2x2 block whose left column is an object color and right column is its halo color.\n- Away from the markers, every source color from the legend appears as one or more 4-connected monochrome objects.\n\nRule:\n- Keep the input pixels unchanged.\n- For each source-color object, take its tight bbox expanded by one cell and clipped to the grid.\n- Recolor background pixels in that expanded region to the marker's halo color, except for background holes enclosed by the object.\n\nKey insight:\n- The small left-edge bars are a legend: they map object colors to the colors used for the surrounding padded bbox.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"4-connected monochrome objects on the background plus left-edge two-column color legend markers\",\n  \"transform\": \"for each object whose color appears in the legend, fill background pixels in its one-cell padded bbox with the paired legend color; preserve the object and any enclosed background holes\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"left-edge two-column legend maps object color to bbox-fill color\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"320afe60\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3813\nmechanism=0.4518\nlexical=0.0102\ncode_feature=0.6000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:ray_loop, object:grid_edge, object:hole, object:path, object:sprite, operation:draw_line, operation:recolor, relation:between, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/320afe60.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/320afe60.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSlide each foreground object horizontally to the edge indicated by whether its shape has an open notch.\n\nInput structure:\n- Yellow is the background and there is one blue foreground color.\n- The foreground is split into separated 4-connected objects.\n- Each object keeps its row span and shape in the output.\n\nRule:\n- If an object's bbox border contains a background gap flanked by object pixels along that same border, slide it to the right edge and recolor it green.\n- Otherwise slide the object to the left edge and recolor it red.\n- Start from a blank background canvas; no moved objects overlap.\n\nKey insight:\n- The target side is encoded by the object's shape, not by its original position: open notches go right, while closed or solid shapes go left.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"4-connected blue foreground objects\",\n  \"path\": \"horizontal slide in the same rows to the selected grid edge\",\n  \"dst\": \"left edge for closed or solid objects; right edge for objects with a flanked open notch on the bbox border\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"translate the whole object without changing its shape\",\n  \"transform\": \"recolor left-moving objects red and right-moving objects green\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"2f767503\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.4015\nmechanism=0.5285\nlexical=0.0105\ncode_feature=0.3333\noverlap_tags=code:connected_components, code:ray_loop, object:grid_edge, object:hole, object:line_segment, object:marker, object:path, object:sprite, operation:draw_line, operation:ray_cast, operation:recolor, relation:direction\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/2f767503.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/2f767503.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nErase each target-color object crossed by the ray pointed by the bar-and-control marker.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- There is one three-pixel straight marker bar and one singleton control pixel adjacent to the bar center.\n- The remaining non-background color forms multiple 4-connected target objects.\n\nRule:\n- Cast a straight ray from the marker bar center in the direction away from the adjacent control pixel.\n- Find every 4-connected target-color object that intersects that ray.\n- Recolor all pixels of those hit target objects to the background; all other pixels stay unchanged.\n\nKey insight:\n- The whole object is erased when the center ray touches any of its pixels; the full marker bar width is not swept.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"three-pixel marker bar with an adjacent singleton control pixel\",\n  \"path\": \"straight center ray from the bar center going away from the control pixel to the grid edge\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"ray itself is not painted; it selects each 4-connected target-color object it crosses\",\n  \"transform\": \"recolor all pixels of selected target objects to background; leave the marker and other target objects unchanged\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"5623160b\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.4080\nmechanism=0.4910\nlexical=0.0105\ncode_feature=0.6000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:ray_loop, object:grid_edge, object:hole, object:marker, object:path, object:sprite, operation:draw_line, operation:ray_cast, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5623160b.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/5623160b.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nPush every colored object touching maroon markers straight outward until it reaches the grid edge.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- Maroon pixels are fixed markers.\n- Every other foreground 4-connected object touches the marker pixels on exactly one cardinal side.\n\nRule:\n- Clear each non-background, non-maroon object from its original position.\n- Translate it in the direction away from its maroon contact until the object reaches the grid boundary.\n- Keep the maroon marker pixels unchanged.\n\nKey insight:\n- The maroon contact side is a launcher: it determines a unique outward ray for the whole object, and the edge of the grid determines the translation distance.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"non-background, non-maroon 4-connected objects touching maroon marker pixels\",\n  \"path\": \"move straight away from the maroon contact side along the matching row or column\",\n  \"dst\": \"furthest in-bounds position where the object reaches the grid edge\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"translate each object once, preserving its shape and color\",\n  \"transform\": \"clear each moving object from its original position; keep maroon markers unchanged\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"9344f635\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3898\nmechanism=0.4642\nlexical=0.0106\ncode_feature=0.6000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:ray_loop, object:grid_edge, object:line_segment, object:marker, object:path, object:sprite, operation:draw_line, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/9344f635.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/9344f635.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nExtend each colored domino marker into a full row or column bar, with horizontal bars covering vertical bars at crossings.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- Every foreground object is a 4-connected same-color domino of exactly two pixels.\n- A horizontal domino marks a row to paint; a vertical domino marks a column to paint.\n\nRule:\n- Paint each marked column entirely with the color of its vertical domino marker.\n- Paint each marked row entirely with the color of its horizontal domino marker.\n- Rows are painted after columns, so row bars overwrite column bars at intersections.\n\nKey insight:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
